WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.258
Step six reads back the tenant
restrictions version two policy,

2
00:00:04.258 --> 00:00:07.275
default and partners,
and writes both to files.

3
00:00:07.275 --> 00:00:09.188
Step seven turns on tagging.

4
00:00:09.188 --> 00:00:13.006
Remember it's tenant-wide: it
acts on everyone the Microsoft

5
00:00:13.006 --> 00:00:16.901
traffic profile carries, which
in this lab is the pilot group.

6
00:00:16.901 --> 00:00:20.850
The GET should show network
packet tagging status enabled.

7
00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:25.982
Step eight runs Learn's four-case test
from the pilot device with the client on:

8
00:00:25.982 --> 00:00:30.313
a member, an allowed partner, a tenant
that isn't allowed, and a guest.

9
00:00:30.313 --> 00:00:31.887
Record each outcome.

10
00:00:31.887 --> 00:00:36.506
Step nine reads the blocks in the
workspace, with Learn's query on error

11
00:00:36.506 --> 00:00:40.887
five million two hundred eleven;
case three's sign-in appears there.

12
00:00:40.887 --> 00:00:45.138
Keep the compliant network policy
in report-only and tagging on.

13
00:00:45.138 --> 00:00:48.480
Module 6 rolls them back,
in the guide's order.
